/// **A window and not a sheet, deliberately.** It has three doors — the
/// editor's Contribute button, Settings' Contribute… button and the automatic ask — and
/// two of them have no document to hold a sheet. It is modal to nothing, so
/// no window and no tool call ever waits on it. `SettingsWindowController`'s
/// mould: one instance, not released when closed, no frame autosave name.
/// It is built from the sheets' own pieces so it reads as one of them, and
/// it is left out of the Window menu because both buttons reopen it.
///
/// **Two ways to show it.** `show()` is a person's press: key and front, and
/// it writes nothing. `showAutomatic()` is the ask Frame Job makes by itself
/// (TIP-4): front WITHOUT key, so a Return typed into the editor can never
/// press "Contribute". The two order calls are closures because a probe's
/// window is never key and could not tell the two apart otherwise.
///
/// **What "Contribute" does.** Opens `TipsLink.url` in the browser, records
/// the press as an ask (TIP-5) and closes. Nothing here knows whether anyone
/// contributed.
final class TipsWindowController: NSWindowController {
    /// The app's one Contribute dialog. A probe builds its own.
/// window is one fixed lockup and remembering where it was is not worth a
/// key. It is NOT `isExcludedFromWindowsMenu`: unlike the queue, nothing in
/// the Window menu opens it, so AppKit's own row is the only way back to a
/// window the person has buried.
///
/// **Five panes, "MCP", "Assistant", "Transcription", "Playback" then "Contributions"**
/// (issue batch B74's `MCPSettingsPane`, spec §11 MC-7; road map 12 A2's
/// `AssistantSettingsPane`; `transcriptionPane`; G-38's
/// `PlaybackSettingsPane`; then TIP-6's `TipsSettingsPane`), each a vertical stack
/// and each one of `content`'s arranged subviews, 24 pt apart through
/// `content.spacing`. §5d's one pane was taken as a HEADING inside a window
/// titled Settings rather than as a tab bar with one tab. The Assistant,
/// Transcription and Playback panes open with `settingsSectionHeader` — a heading and a
/// `SettingsInfoButton` whose popover holds its explanation (spec §11 SH-5);
/// the MCP pane opens with its bare heading and shows its blurb, because
/// MC-7 asked for the text above its button, and the Contributions pane with its bare
/// heading and one sentence (TIP-6). There is still a Transcription
/// section, so the sentence the `transcribe` tool and its catalog entry both
/// print — the one that sends a caller to Settings and then to Transcription
            viewCluster(),
            DividerView(length: Self.toolbarDividerLength),
            AccentButton(
                title: "Export…", symbol: "square.and.arrow.up", fallback: "⤴",
                tooltip: "Export… (⌘E)", action: #selector(exportProject(_:))),
            // The Contribute button, an experiment (spec §11 TIP-6); it hides itself while its toggle is off.
            TipsToolbarButton(),
        ])
        row.translatesAutoresizingMaskIntoConstraints = false
    /// is no options at all, so a caller that says nothing exports what it
    /// always did.
    ///
    /// This is a person's export, so its success is told to `tips` (spec §11
    /// TIP-4): counted then, and the Contribute dialog shown, when it is due, once
    /// this window's result sheet has ended.
    func beginExport(
        settings: ExportSettings, to url: URL, options: RecipeOptions = .none,
        tips: TipsDoors = .shared
    static let coral = NSColor(srgbRed: 0xF4 / 255, green: 0x65 / 255, blue: 0x3F / 255, alpha: 1)

    /// The editor toolbar's Contribute button (spec §11 TIP-6): a leaf green, the
    /// same in both appearances, under a white label at 5.1:1. Not `forest`,
    /// which is within 10/255 of the action ink's light value, and not
    /// `action` itself (CI-4): this one sits about 40° of hue from both.
    static let tips = NSColor(srgbRed: 0x2E / 255, green: 0x7D / 255, blue: 0x32 / 255, alpha: 1)

